  "content": "## Overview\n\nA **UUID** (Universally Unique Identifier) or **GUID** (Globally Unique Identifier) is a 128-bit label used to uniquely identify information in computer systems. Version 4 UUIDs are generated using cryptographically secure random numbers, providing essentially zero chance of collision.\n\nOur browser-native **UUID Generator** executes entirely on your device using the W3C Web Cryptography API (`crypto.randomUUID` and `crypto.getRandomValues`). No identifiers are logged or sent across the network.\n\n---\n\n## Anatomy of a Version 4 UUID\n\nA standard UUID v4 consists of 32 hexadecimal digits displayed in 5 groups separated by hyphens in the format `8-4-4-4-12` (total 36 characters):\n```\nxxxxxxxx-xxxx-4xxx-yxxx-xxxxxxxxxxxx\n```\n- The **4** at the start of the third group specifies Version 4 (randomly generated).\n- The **y** in the fourth group encodes the variant bits (`8`, `9`, `a`, or `b`).\n- Out of 128 bits, 6 bits are reserved for version and variant metadata, leaving **122 bits of pure cryptographic entropy**.\n\n---\n\n## Collision Probability: Can Two UUIDs Collide?\n\nThe total number of possible UUID v4 values is approximately 5.3 x 10^36. To put this astronomical number into perspective:\n- If you generated **1 billion UUIDs every single second** for 100 years, the probability of creating a duplicate is less than 0.0000000001%.\n- Generating duplicate UUIDs by chance is virtually impossible in any software architecture.\n\n---\n\n## Step-by-Step Instructions\n\n1. **Select Quantity**: Choose how many UUIDs to generate at once (from 1 up to 100).\n2. **Configure Format**: Toggle uppercase/lowercase and whether hyphens or braces should be included.\n3. **Generate**: Click **Generate UUIDs** to run the Web Crypto RNG.\n4. **Copy**: Click **Copy** to grab an individual UUID or **Copy All** to export the entire list.\n\n---\n\n## Best Practices in Software Engineering\n\n- **Primary Keys in Distributed Databases**: Using UUIDs allows client applications or microservices to generate unique record IDs independently without round-trip coordination with a central database sequence.\n- **Security & Randomness**: Never generate UUIDs with pseudo-random generators like Math.random(). Always use cryptographically secure sources like crypto.randomUUID().\n- **Formatting Consistency**: Standardize on lowercase hyphenated strings in REST APIs and JSON schemas."
