  "content": "## Overview\n\nIn HTML, certain characters are reserved by the parser for markup syntax (such as `<` and `>` for opening and closing tags). When raw text contains these symbols, the browser interprets them as HTML tags rather than text content.\n\n**HTML Entity Encoding** replaces reserved and special characters with predefined character references, ensuring safe display and preventing **Cross-Site Scripting (XSS)** vulnerabilities.\n\nOur **HTML Entity Converter** runs locally in your browser to instantly encode or decode HTML entities with zero data leakage.\n\n---\n\n## Why HTML Escaping is Critical for Web Security\n\nUnsanitized user input rendered directly into the DOM is the leading cause of Cross-Site Scripting (XSS) attacks. For example, if a comment form accepts raw script tags, direct rendering allows an attacker to execute malicious scripts inside other users' sessions. When HTML-escaped, this string transforms into safe entities:\n```html\n&lt;script&gt;alert(document.cookie)&lt;/script&gt;\n```\nThe browser displays the exact characters without interpreting or executing the code.\n\n---\n\n## Standard Named HTML Entities\n\n| Raw Character | Named Entity | Decimal Entity | Hex Entity | Description |\n|:---:|:---:|:---:|:---:|:---|\n| `&` | `&amp;` | `&#38;` | `&#x26;` | Ampersand |\n| `<` | `&lt;` | `&#60;` | `&#x3C;` | Less-than sign |\n| `>` | `&gt;` | `&#62;` | `&#x3E;` | Greater-than sign |\n| `\"` | `&quot;` | `&#34;` | `&#x22;` | Double quotation mark |\n| `'` | `&#39;` | `&#39;` | `&#x27;` | Apostrophe / Single quote |\n| Space | `&nbsp;` | `&#160;` | `&#xA0;` | Non-breaking space |\n| `©` | `&copy;` | `&#169;` | `&#xA9;` | Copyright symbol |\n| `™` | `&trade;` | `&#8482;` | `&#2122;` | Trademark symbol |\n\n---\n\n## Step-by-Step Instructions\n\n1. **Choose Mode**: Toggle **Encode** (convert raw text to HTML entities) or **Decode** (convert entities back to plain text).\n2. **Input Text**: Type or paste your HTML or code snippets into the input field.\n3. **Live Conversion**: See the escaped or unescaped text generated instantly.\n4. **Copy**: Click **Copy Result** to paste the sanitized text into your templates or documentation."
